      "text": "To determine the value of \\( v \\) such that \\( \\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10} \\) is a root of the quadratic equation \\( 5x^2 + 21x + v = 0 \\), we can use the fact that if \\( \\alpha \\) is a root of the quadratic equation \\( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \\), then \\( \\alpha \\) satisfies the equation \\( a\\alpha^2 + b\\alpha + c = 0 \\).\n\nHere, the quadratic equation is \\( 5x^2 + 21x + v = 0 \\), so if \\( \\alpha = \\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10} \\) is a root, then:\n\n\\[ 5\\left(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2 + 21\\left(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right) + v = 0. \\]\n\nFirst, let's calculate \\( \\left(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2 \\):\n\n\\[ \\left(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\right)^2 = \\frac{(-21-\\sqrt{301})^2}{100} = \\frac{441 + 42\\sqrt{301} + 301}{100} = \\frac{742 + 42\\sqrt{301}}{100}. \\]\n\nNext, we substitute this back into the equation:\n\n\\[ 5 \\cdot \\frac{742 + 42\\sqrt{301}}{100} + 21 \\cdot \\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10} + v = 0. \\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\n\\[ \\frac{5(742 + 42\\sqrt{301})}{100} + \\frac{21(-21 - \\sqrt{301})}{10} + v = 0, \\]\n\\[ \\frac{3710 + 210\\sqrt{301}}{100} + \\frac{-441 - 21\\sqrt{301}}{10} + v = 0, \\]\n\\[ \\frac{3710 + 210\\sqrt{301}}{100} + \\frac{-4410 - 210\\sqrt{301}}{100} + v = 0, \\]\n\\[ \\frac{3710 - 4410}{100} + \\frac{210\\sqrt{301} - 210\\sqrt{301}}{100} + v = 0, \\]\n\\[ \\frac{-700}{100} + v = 0, \\]\n\\[ -7 + v = 0, \\]\n\\[ v = 7. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( v \\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
