      "text": "To solve for the real value of \\( v \\) such that \\(\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}\\) is a root of the quadratic equation \\(5x^2 + 21x + v = 0\\), we can use the fact that if \\( r \\) is a root of the quadratic equation \\( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \\), then \\( a r^2 + b r + c = 0 \\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ r = \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\]\n\\[ 5x^2 + 21x + v = 0 \\]\n\nWe substitute \\( r \\) into the quadratic equation:\n\\[ 5 \\left( \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\right)^2 + 21 \\left( \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\right) + v = 0 \\]\n\nFirst, simplify \\( \\left( \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\right)^2 \\):\n\\[ \\left( \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\right)^2 = \\frac{(-21 - \\sqrt{301})^2}{100} = \\frac{441 + 2 \\cdot (-21) \\cdot \\sqrt{301} + 301}{100} = \\frac{441 - 42 \\sqrt{301} + 301}{100} = \\frac{742 - 42 \\sqrt{301}}{100} = \\frac{371 - 21 \\sqrt{301}}{50} \\]\n\nNow substitute this back into the quadratic equation:\n\\[ 5 \\left( \\frac{371 - 21 \\sqrt{301}}{50} \\right) + 21 \\left( \\frac{-21 - \\sqrt{301}}{10} \\right) + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{5(371 - 21 \\sqrt{301})}{50} + \\frac{21(-21 - \\sqrt{301})}{10} + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{5(371 - 21 \\sqrt{301})}{50} = \\frac{1855 - 105 \\sqrt{301}}{50} = \\frac{1855}{50} - \\frac{105 \\sqrt{301}}{50} = 37.1 - 2.1 \\sqrt{301} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{21(-21 - \\sqrt{301})}{10} = \\frac{-441 - 21 \\sqrt{301}}{10} = -44.1 - 2.1 \\sqrt{301} \\]\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\\[ 37.1 - 2.1 \\sqrt{301} - 44.1 - 2.1 \\sqrt{301} + v = 0 \\]\n\\[ -7 + v - 4.2 \\sqrt{301} = 0 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( v \\):\n\\[ v = 7 + 4.2 \\sqrt{301} \\]\n\nLet's compute the final value of \\( v \\) using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Given value\r\nr = (-21 - math.sqrt(301)) / 10\r\n\r\n# Calculate v\r\nv = 7 + 4.2 * math.sqrt(301)\r\nprint(v)\n```\n```output\n117.03400610112143\n```\nThe final value of \\( v \\) is approximately \\( 117.034 \\). However, for exact representation, the value is:\n\n\